  "review_notes": [
    "Corrected: the impersonal 'it' of 'if it seem good' is added under rule 20's cleft/impersonal-it sentence; the ASV writes 'good' for טָב without any frame elsewhere, so by rule 20's own test the frame is supplied rather than the predicate's fixed rendering. The linking verb 'seem' stays with the predicate as the construction-supplied copula.",
    "וּכְעַן → 'Now therefore' divides per rule 14's וְעַתָּה example; 'the king's treasure house' follows rule 29's possessive case with דִּי inside the possessive."
